    [34mlet[39m id = localStorage.[33mgetItem[39m([31m"login-tracking-id"[39m);
    [34mif[39m (!id) {
      id = crypto.[33mrandomUUID[39m();
      localStorage.[33msetItem[39m([31m"login-tracking-id"[39m, id);
    }
    [34mreturn[39m id;
  }

  Then [38;5;153mlogin[39m takes it as a third positional parameter, logs it, and echoes it in the result so downstream consumers of
  the return value can see it:

  [34mfunction[39m [33mlogin[39m(username, password, userId) {
    console.[33mlog[39m([31m"Logging in:"[39m, username, [31m"userId:"[39m, userId);
    [34mreturn[39m { [36msuccess[39m: [34mtrue[39m, [36muser[39m: username, userId };
  }

  And the submit handler at [38;5;153mapp.js:23[39m becomes [38;5;153mlogin(username, password, getTrackingId())[39m.

  [1mDecisions inside that[0m

  - [1mThird positional, always passed.[0m One caller, so there's no compatibility reason to make it optional. If it were
    optional, the tracking would silently no-op whenever someone forgot it — a required-in-practice parameter fails
    visibly instead.
  - [1m[38;5;153mcrypto.randomUUID()[0m needs a secure context (https or localhost). Opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m as a [38;5;153mfile://[39m URL will throw. Say
    the word if you need a fallback; I'd rather not add one speculatively.
  - [1mEchoed in the return value[0m so the id travels with the result rather than living only in a log line.

  [1mFiles touched:[0m [38;5;153mapp.js[39m only. No change to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m.

  [1mTesting:[0m nothing automated — I'd verify by loading the page, submitting the form, and confirming the console shows a
  stable id across reloads. I'm not scaffolding a test runner for this unless you want one.

